  "verbalization": "Nifedipine is implicated in the regulation of Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2 through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is directly linked to Natural resistance-associated macrophage protein 2, which in turn is a target of Npc133119, and Npc133119 further targets the aminopeptidase. This suggests a chain of interactions where Nifedipine influences the expression or activity of a protein that ultimately affects the aminopeptidase. Additionally, Nifedipine is also linked to IMR-32, a cell line that is a target of Hesperidin, which also targets the aminopeptidase. These findings collectively indicate that Nifedipine may modulate the activity of the aminopeptidase through a series of molecular intermediates, possibly involving cellular signaling or protein regulation. The evidence supports a mechanism where Nifedipine indirectly influences the aminopeptidase via a network of targets, highlighting the complexity of its pharmacological effects.",
